==Enemy==
Rain D. is a large, fast-moving enemy with moderately high health. At 100% strength magnification, his headbutt attacks deal about 5,000 damage each. Rain D. also has a notoriously high knockback count and deceptively long range (300) along with a fast attack rate, making him quite the threat when guarded by and supporting enemies with few to no knockbacks as he can easily hit them while staying away from your line of fire. What makes him even worse is his powerful support abilities, as he can be spammed, spawned with other equally annoying threats or both.

Although intimidating when buffed, this enemy becomes somewhat easier to deal with later on in the game due to an abundance of [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]]/[[:Category:Omni Strike Cats|Omni Strike]]/[[:Category:Wave Attack Cats|Wave]]/[[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surge]]/[[:Category:Explosion Cats|Explosion]] cats such as [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Hacker Cat]], [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Polevaulter Cat]] and [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Sexy Legs Cat]], which can consistently hit him from behind cover.

==Strategy==
To stall Rain D., use a few units that deal enough damage to knock him back while outranging him, such as [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Sexy Legs Cat]], or [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]], so that he doesn't quickly shred your defenses before you store up enough cash to deploy heavier hitters such as [[Valkyrie Cat (Special Cat)|True Valkyrie Cat]] or [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]]. Sending [[Cat (Normal Cat)|the]] [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|cheapest]] [[Gold Cat (Super Rare Cat)|meatshields]] (75¢) on different intervals can help to effectively stall Rain D. while accumulating cash.

His knockback count can be annoying or helpful in the right situation. It allows him to reposition, but if constant damage is dealt to him, he will be stun-locked and can't even attack for a good while. A good example of units that can do this are [[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|Surge Attackers]], such as [[Kasli the Scourge (Uber Rare Cat)|Ritual Saint Kasli]] and [[Brainwashed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Sexy Legs Cat]], provided if the Surge has just enough damage to juggle him consistently. If one stalls his attack with a meatshield, in stages like [[Hungry Forest]], Awakened Bahamut can either rip massive shreds of HP or straight up end him.

When fighting groups of Rain Ds in stages like [[Scorched Tollbooth]], it helps to sync them up in front of the [[Cat Base]] before rushing them down with [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attackers]].

