==Trivia==
*Rain D.'s Japanese name, Nakai-kun (ナカイくん), is derived from 馴鹿 ''tonakai'' (reindeer). It's also a reference to the leader of [[wikipedia:SMAP|SMAP]], [[wikipedia:Masahiro Nakai|Masahiro Nakai]], who had a television program named ''Nakai-kun Onsen'' and likes baseball and singing, just like Rain D. in the [[Nyanko Daisensou|Japanese Version]].
*According to his Japanese description, Rain D. may actually be a person wearing a reindeer costume.
*Rain D. and [[Midnite D.]] are cousins.

